<section class="card"><h2><?= e(t('How the connection works')) ?></h2><ol><li><?= e(t('Add the website URL, optional business name, server details and technology in LifeOS.')) ?></li><li><?= e(t('Install the matching PHP, WordPress or Next.js adapter, or implement the same API in your backend.')) ?></li><li><?= e(t('Configure the adapter on your server. Keep credentials private; the PHP package creates website accounts, WordPress uses Application Passwords, and the Next.js example uses a server-side API token.')) ?></li><li><?= e(t('Enter the HTTPS connector endpoint in LifeOS, then use the sign-in method described by that adapter. Its declared collections generate the forms and record views.')) ?></li><li><?= e(t('Repeat for all your websites. Switch between them from All websites or the website switcher. Each website keeps its own session and permissions.')) ?></li><li><?= e(t('Load records, review changes, and save to that website. Sign out when finished.')) ?></li></ol><a class="btn secondary" href="/websites/connector/download" hx-boost="false"><?= e(t('Download connector & protocol guide')) ?></a><p class="footnote"><?= e(t('The reference connector has its own content store and a public read helper. Your public website must read that content, or its adapter must write to the website\'s existing backend. Deploying a connector alone does not rewrite an existing site.')) ?></p></section>
